   "source": [
    "# Project Cutoff \u2014 Credit Policy Design for Meridian Capital\n",
    "**STRATIFY 2.0 | Business Analytics Bootcamp, Analytics Club & Consult Club, UGAC, IIT Bombay**\n",
    "\n",
    "Meridian Capital currently approves 29% of loan applications. Bad loans have risen from 3.1% to 4.6%,\n",
    "and the board wants a data-backed answer on what approval rate Meridian should run in FY27 \u2014 one that\n",
    "maximises profit while keeping the default rate at or below **6.5%**.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook works through the two tasks in the brief:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Rule diagnosis** \u2014 quantify what each of the 8 current rejection rules is costing or saving Meridian,\n",
    "   both in isolation and in exclusive (non-overlapping) terms.\n",
    "2. **Approval-rate optimisation** \u2014 using the applicant risk score, find the approval rate that makes the\n",
    "   most profit without breaching the 6.5% default cap.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Contents**\n",
    "1. Data & current policy\n",
    "2. Rule-level financial diagnosis (each rule in isolation)\n",
    "3. Rule impact without overlap (solo-rejected applicants)\n",
    "4. Does the risk score actually work? \u2014 cumulative default rate & profit by band\n",
    "5. Loan economics \u2014 profit and loss per loan\n",
    "6. Finding the best approval rate (1% resolution, zoomed into the band identified in Section 4)\n",
    "7. Recommended policy vs. today's policy\n",
    "8. Answers for the board\n"
   ]
  },
