    "## 2. Rule-Level Financial Diagnosis \u2014 Each Rule In Isolation (Task 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "For each rule **on its own**, we ask: *if this rule alone decided who gets rejected, what would it cost\n",
    "or save Meridian?* This ignores whether the same applicant also trips other rules.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "foregone profit  = (rejected by this rule AND would have repaid)     x  profit per good loan\n",
    "avoided loss      = (rejected by this rule AND would have defaulted)  x  loss per bad loan\n",
    "net impact        = avoided loss \u2212 foregone profit\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Important:** because rules overlap (one applicant can trip several at once), the *rejected* counts below\n",
    "are **not mutually exclusive** and cannot be summed into a single policy total. Section 3 fixes that by\n",
    "isolating each rule's *exclusive* (solo) impact.\n",
    "\n",
    "(Profit/loss constants are derived in Section 5; brought forward here to build this table.)"
   ]
