    "## 3. Rule Impact Without Overlap \u2014 Solo-Rejected Applicants\n",
    "\n",
    "Section 2 treats each rule independently, so its counts overlap with the other rules and can't be\n",
    "added up. Here we isolate the applicants rejected by **exactly one rule** \u2014 the rule that, on its own,\n",
    "is the *sole* reason that applicant is rejected. These solo-rejected groups **are** mutually exclusive\n",
    "by construction, so their counts can be compared and summed directly.\n",
    "\n",
    "This tells us which rule is genuinely doing independent work versus which rules mostly reject people\n",
    "who were already going to be rejected by something else anyway."
   ]
