   "source": [
    "## 4. Does the Risk Score Actually Work? \u2014 Cumulative Default Rate & Profit by Band\n",
    "\n",
    "`risk_score` is provided in the data \u2014 a predicted probability of default (0 = safest, 1 = riskiest).\n",
    "Before trusting it to set a cutoff, we check two things at increasing approval levels:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Does the default rate climb as we approve more people?** (confirms the score ranks risk correctly)\n",
    "2. **Where does the default rate cross Meridian's 6.5% ceiling, and what is profit doing at that point?**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Method:** sort every applicant safest \u2192 riskiest by `risk_score`, split into **20 bands of 5% each**\n",
    "(Band 1 = safest 5%, Band 20 = riskiest 5%), then for each band compute:\n",
    "- the default rate **within just that band**, and\n",
    "- the **cumulative** default rate and profit if Meridian approved everyone from Band 1 up through that\n",
    "  band (i.e., approving the safest 5%, then 10%, then 15%, and so on)."
   ]
  },
